{
  "requirement": "Validation MUST read the mdBook source directory from `[book].src` in `book.toml`, using `src` when the setting is absent. It MUST report an unreadable or malformed book configuration and reject an empty, absolute, or parent-traversing source path.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Verdict: true.** The implementation covers every obligation in `requirements.ci.book_source`, and the unit test covers the interesting cases. I found two minor points that I did not treat as gaps.\n\n**Implementation.** `book_source_dir` in `src/evidence.rs` (lines 297–348) is marked `{impl}` for this requirement.\n- **Read and default:** it reads `book.toml` and takes `[book].src`. It uses `\"src\"` only when `[book]` or `src` is absent. It accepts both `[book]` tables and inline `book = { ... }` tables through `as_table_like`.\n- **Unreadable or malformed configuration:** it reports \"cannot read book configuration\", \"invalid TOML\", \"book must be a table\", and \"book.src must be a string\" as errors.\n- **Path rejection:** it rejects an empty source, and any source whose components are not all `Normal` or `CurDir`. That rejects absolute paths, Windows prefixes, and `..` anywhere in the path, including `md/../outside`.\n- **Where errors surface:** `load_definitions` (marked `{impl}`, line 139) and `inspect_repository_with_progress` (line 170) both call it. The validation report built by `validate_repository` and the status and index paths therefore include these errors.\n\n**Tests.** `book_source_defaults_only_when_absent_and_reports_invalid_configuration` (line 1421) is marked `{test}` and covers these cases:\n- **Default and explicit source:** an empty file, `[book]` without `src`, `src='docs'`, and an inline `book = {src=...}` table.\n- **Missing file:** `book.toml` removed.\n- **Malformed TOML:** `[book` is reported as invalid TOML.\n- **Wrong types:** a non-table `book` is reported, and so are integer, boolean, array and table values for `src`.\n- **Rejected paths:** empty, absolute, `../outside`, and `md/../outside`.\n\n`validates_full_names_requirement_text_and_input_lines` (line 1474) exercises the whole validation path with a valid configuration. Nearly all other fixtures also set `src = 'md'`.\n\n**Minor observations, not treated as gaps.**\n- The call site in `inspect_repository_with_progress` is not marked `{impl}` for this requirement, although `load_definitions` is. It is only plumbing around the marked function, so I do not count it as unmarked implementation.\n- After a configuration error the function returns `root.join(\"md\")` as a fallback so that discovery can continue. This is not stated in the requirement, but it is consistent with `requirements.ci.errors` (continue after a failed check) and it does not change which errors are reported.\n- No test drives an invalid `book.toml` through `validate_repository` end to end. The unit test on `book_source_dir` covers the logic, and the wiring is a direct call that pushes into the shared error list.",
